id: SCA-044
title: Suspicious go.mod replace directive pointing to remote
category: supply-chain
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  filenames: go.mod
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: replace\s+\S+\s+=>\s+(github\.com|gitlab\.com|bitbucket\.org|[a-z]+\.[a-z]+/)
    message: Remote replace directive can redirect a trusted module to an attacker-controlled repository, serving backdoored code transparently.
fix: Remote replace directives should only be used temporarily during development. Remove before merging. Use go mod tidy to clean up.
